# `core::primitives::bool` -- `bool`'s declaration site.
#
# One bit of information, stored in one byte. Its operators are `==`/`!=` and
# `&`/`|`/`^` -- and since this language has no `&&`/`||`/`!`, those three
# *are* its logical operators, evaluating both operands rather than
# short-circuiting.
#
# Ordering (`<`), arithmetic (`+`), the shifts and `~` are all rejected:
# `bool` has no `arithmetic_repr`, so unlike pointers it never
# decays to an integer to make an operator work. It is a truth value, not a
# zero-or-one.
primitive bool { }
